{"about_the_game":"<h2 class=\"bb_tag\">WHAT IS THIS GAME?</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Pixel Transit is a game where you construct a transit system in an infinitely vast, tile-based world. Each tile serves a distinct function\u2014for example, sidewalk tiles allow pedestrians to walk, train track tiles guide trains, and road tiles accommodate cars.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">TRANSIT MECHANICS</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">When a new person is introduced to the world, they begin by randomly searching for a building on the map. If they locate one, they will attempt to reach it as fast as possible using the network of sidewalks, trains, or cars built by the player. So, people like to choose to get on trains even when the train route is longer than the walking path if they think it's more efficient.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3588930/extras/transit.png?t=1745203128\" /></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">HEALTH AND RECOVERY</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Every person has a health meter that, if it falls below zero, results in death. Reaching a building fully restores their health. Additionally, resting rooms can help recover health, though their capacity is limited. Since walking rapidly decreases health, it is advisable to keep people on trains or cars\u2014or to build plenty of resting rooms to ensure their survival.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3588930/extras/restroom.png?t=1745203128\" /></p>","achievements":{"highlighted":[{"name":"EVILMODE","path":"https://cdn.akamai.steamstatic.com/steamcommunity/public/images/apps/3588930/ac84dd98cdfb472588b7102f537c47f94a544901.jpg"}],"total":1},"background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3588930?t=1745203128","background_raw":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3588930/665a000c90d11